{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/968396-the-furry-thread","id":968396,"title":"The Furry Thread","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-12T23:57:36-07:00","id":968396,"title":"The Furry Thread","content":"So this is probably a terrible idea, but here it goes.<br /> <br /> It's been weird to see things shift regarding furries on the internet, going from the &quot;yiff in hell&quot; nonsense from the mid-2000s to seeing the massive outpouring of creative content in the past few years. <a href=\"https://spacetwinks.itch.io/everyones-a-furry-2k16\" target=\"_blank\">This </a>little retrospective made for an interesting read on the history of things in the fandom and helped underscore a point I hadn't consciously thought of before: the furry community is a huge safe space for queer experimentation, and allows people across the internet to be curious about their sexualities and gender identities through an extra layer of anonymity and separation - much like I've heard time and time again about tabletop roleplaying! - and it's a narrative you hear consistently from people. I'm personally wrestling with a lot of gender issues myself, and the ability to take a step back and have a character who knows she's a transgender woman (even if I don't for sure, or can't safely explore it myself due to where I am) has been a <i>huge</i> outlet for how stressful all this is.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure what I want this thread to do, and I'm scared it'll either go without replies or become moderator city like some of the LGBTQ threads have been unfortunate enough to be, but I figure it's a topic that likely has some crossover with the community here; when you spend your time pretending to be vampires, fairies, and godlings, pretending to be a fox man or a cow lady doesn't seem as outre as it would elsewhere. <br /> <br /> Does anyone else here have experiences with the whole furry phenomenon, or have any characters they'd like to share? I'd obviously prefer this not become a gigantic dump of porn, bad art, and fetish sex stories, but things will probably take a mature turn. I'm curious to see where this winds up!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T03:04:10-07:00","id":968433,"title":"","content":"I must admit I don't know much about that community, not being part of it myself, but everything that helps people to experiment and find themselves in a safe eviroment counts with my support. I'll read the article and maybe comment more later.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I don't think it was a bad idea to create thread, quite the contrary, hope people remain civil. The little I know about furries is that they are usually treated with much disdain.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T12:02:35-07:00","id":968663,"title":"","content":"I have friends that are in various levels of furrydom, and I've always found the mockery and stereotyping of them rather annoying, Especially because so many of them do not consider it a sexual thing in the slightest.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure I have much to add, or to respond to, so I'll just share a story about one of the reasons I'm very grateful for my furry friends:<br /> <br /> One time I was at an unrelated convention that a friend who's a furry. I got very upset after something that happened, and my friend came over to my room. We just sat together on the bed, watching TV, as I pet them on the head. It was one of the flat out most relaxing nights of my life. It was all of the soothing sensations of relaxing with a pet, with all the emotional support of a friend you can actually talk to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T12:18:40-07:00","id":968669,"title":"","content":"I have some furry tendencies that grew out my love of werewolves and other human to animal/ animal to human shapeshifters. The way I see it, the number of housewives that read werewolf erotica (to the point of there being multiple sub genres of it) means that maybe furry tendencies are more common than most people think","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T14:16:24-07:00","id":968734,"title":"","content":"I've always felt I've had a somewhat distant yet tangential and mutually respectful relationship with the concept of furry. The fact that I'm not particularly appreciative of animals in general doesn't help, of course. I don't consider myself a furry, but I mean, look at my avatar. I'm clearly somewhere on the spectrum.<br /> <br /> Animals have served as reflections of humanity since the earliest time. The aboriginal stories and the fables of Aesop all feature animals with human behaviour. Enkidu from the Epic of Gilgamesh is a half-beast. Hell, almost all the classic Disney characters are are straight up furries, the lot of them. I've never seen a reason that this would suddenly become objectionable. I suppose my stance is &quot;live and let live&quot;. It's not for me to participate in consciously, but I can appreciate work that the furry fandom creates and if I really analysed myself, I'm sure I could find tendencies in myself as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T15:23:36-07:00","id":968781,"title":"","content":"While I've certainly witnessed my fair share of furry-bashing (having been on the internet at least once in the last decade) I've also observed that pretty much every single online community I've ever been a part of has had at least a small cluster of furries in it. This has run the gamut from Harry Potter, Star Trek, D&amp;D, anime, Magic the Gathering, all variety of forum roleplays and browser games, to stuff like horror fandom, conspiracy theories, and alternate history. Not always large, not always accepted, but pretty much always there and at least somewhat visible. <br /> <br /> By odd coincidence a good sized chunk of the gaming community I came up in when I started with White Wolf were also part of the furry community. In only one case was one of them really ostracized, and the role that his status as a furry played in that is even now sort of difficult to unpack. It was primarily due to persistent disruptive behavioral problems, but since parallel to that was the fact that being a furry formed a preponderant and very outward part of his identity it was hard to dissociate or disentangle his behavioral from that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T16:49:00-07:00","id":969532,"title":"","content":"I might as well share my own character, since that's kinda what this thread is for! I recently caved in and made a fursona for myself after years of appreciating other's furry works, and created Keftiu: she's a transwoman, a cow, an employee at a (possibly cursed) antique shop, and the author of an amateur food truck review blog. While I'm really proud of her design, the main thing is having a safe outlet for my own gender expression since I'm uncertain and the place I'm in is pretty hostile. She's also my current icon!<br /> <br /> EDIT: Ack, image embedding is busted on mobile. Have a (sfw, don't worry) <a href=\"http://imgur.com/a/UYKWZ\" target=\"_blank\">link</a> instead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":281,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","user":"atamajakki","date":". 09-15-2016, 02:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T04:57:28-07:00","id":969824,"title":"","content":"I never really got into furry, though several of my close friends in real life are furries, so I don't have anything against furries. While it's not my cup of tea, I still don't understand the intense levels of vitriolic hatred the fandom gets online.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T11:42:05-07:00","id":970803,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Camilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/968396-the-furry-thread?p=969824#post969824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I never really got into furry, though several of my close friends in real life are furries, so I don't have anything against furries. While it's not my cup of tea, I still don't understand the intense levels of vitriolic hatred the fandom gets online.</div> </div> </div> </div>Primarily because so much of the material produced by the furry community is so sexually explicit, to the point that &quot;furry is a sexual fetish&quot; is the reality, not just to many members of the furry community, but to many people whose only knowledge of the furry community is pornographic pictures and stories about fur-suit orgies. Sadly I have noticed that furries, far more so than other online fetishistic communities, tend to be rather eager to throw their kink in your face and are often more dramatic about it than members of other fetishistic communities. It's sort of like how people might not appreciate members of say, the BDSM community coming into a board and posting pictures or discussing their particularly kink where there's no real relevance.<br /> <br /> And it's not really fair to most of the members of the furry community who aren't particularly aggressive with their hobby, that it has been tarred by a relatively small but incredibly vocal group of members, but that's just basically what happened and why the furry community is treated as persona non grata by much of the internet, even by groups whose fetishes and sexual inclinations are much, much stranger in comparison.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T13:51:18-07:00","id":970895,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/968396-the-furry-thread?p=970803#post970803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Primarily because so much of the material produced by the furry community is so sexually explicit, to the point that &quot;furry is a sexual fetish&quot; is the reality, not just to many members of the furry community, but to many people whose only knowledge of the furry community is pornographic pictures and stories about fur-suit orgies. Sadly I have noticed that furries, far more so than other online fetishistic communities, tend to be rather eager to throw their kink in your face and are often more dramatic about it than members of other fetishistic communities. It's sort of like how people might not appreciate members of say, the BDSM community coming into a board and posting pictures or discussing their particularly kink where there's no real relevance.<br /> <br /> And it's not really fair to most of the members of the furry community who aren't particularly aggressive with their hobby, that it has been tarred by a relatively small but incredibly vocal group of members, but that's just basically what happened and why the furry community is treated as persona non grata by much of the internet, even by groups whose fetishes and sexual inclinations are much, much stranger in comparison.</div> </div> </div> </div> \u200bFair point. I knew about some of the fetish stuff via pop culture osmosis, but never really encountered it personally among the few furries I know IRL. Since I never looked into it, I never knew that it had gotten that bad all because of a vocal minority.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T17:21:47-07:00","id":971003,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/968396-the-furry-thread?p=970803#post970803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Primarily because so much of the material produced by the furry community is so sexually explicit, to the point that &amp;quot;furry is a sexual fetish&amp;quot; is the reality, not just to many members of the furry community, but to many people whose only knowledge of the furry community is pornographic pictures and stories about fur-suit orgies. Sadly I have noticed that furries, far more so than other online fetishistic communities, tend to be rather eager to throw their kink in your face and are often more dramatic about it than members of other fetishistic communities. It's sort of like how people might not appreciate members of say, the BDSM community coming into a board and posting pictures or discussing their particularly kink where there's no real relevance.<br /> <br /> And it's not really fair to most of the members of the furry community who aren't particularly aggressive with their hobby, that it has been tarred by a relatively small but incredibly vocal group of members, but that's just basically what happened and why the furry community is treated as persona non grata by much of the internet, even by groups whose fetishes and sexual inclinations are much, much stranger in comparison.</div> </div> </div> </div>It does the community as a whole a disservice to dismiss the whole thing as a fetish: tons of furry creative content is nonsexual in nature, and many fans don't like any of that! It's worth noting that the majority of fursuits aren't built for sex and there's a stark divide among fursuiters between them and the sexual minority.<br /> <br /> But beyond that, it seems a little silly to demonize the sexual elements of the fandom. At worst, it's as goofy as any other kink, and at best it's a safe outlet for experimentation - I'm using my character to work through a lot of gender dysphoria, and feeling comfortable in an avatar of myself being sexual is a huge step forward for me as a whole.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T18:14:15-07:00","id":971041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/968396-the-furry-thread?p=971003#post971003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It does the community as a whole a disservice to dismiss the whole thing as a fetish: tons of furry creative content is nonsexual in nature, and many fans don't like any of that! It's worth noting that the majority of fursuits aren't built for sex and there's a stark divide among fursuiters between them and the sexual minority.<br /> <br /> But beyond that, it seems a little silly to demonize the sexual elements of the fandom. At worst, it's as goofy as any other kink, and at best it's a safe outlet for experimentation - I'm using my character to work through a lot of gender dysphoria, and feeling comfortable in an avatar of myself being sexual is a huge step forward for me as a whole.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a lot of of good things the furry fandom does for its fans (as can be said by members of any fandom), and I'm certainly not trying to demonize the fandom (I don't have a dog in that race way way or another). I was just responding to Camilla's query, explaining that the furry fandom is closely intertwined with sexuality and sexual/gender themes in the minds of a lot of people, both for good and for ill and that's a large part of the reason why it <i>is</i> demonized by so many people.<br /> <br /> It's probably not fair, but for a lot of people the extent of their interactions with the furry community is seeing furry porn, so in their minds it's basically a fetishistic fandom. It's sort of like how pornographic magazines are a big and very visible part of Japan's doujinshi market, to the point that many non-Japanese (who have heard of the term) think that doujinshi means &quot;porn magazine.&quot; Most people who don't know much about furries are probably going to have similar misconceptions because the sexually charged artwork is so <i>loud</i> it tends to drown out other aspects of the fandom.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T18:19:47-07:00","id":971047,"title":"","content":"Hunh. While I have seen furry porn, I am not the least under the impression that the sexual aspects of furry fandom are all that common.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T22:23:04-07:00","id":971160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>etherial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/968396-the-furry-thread?p=971047#post971047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hunh. While I have seen furry porn, I am not the least under the impression that the sexual aspects of furry fandom are all that common.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not gonna deny that a fairly massive chunk of the art out there is pornographic, but I'm also not sure that has to be a bad thing. The awesome person, Spacetwinks, behind the timeline in my OP had this to say in response to a later question about it, which nicely handles things; in other words, the talk shouldn't be &quot;not all furry stuff is porn!&quot; but rather &quot;why is it bad if so much of it is?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ask:Is furry fandom indistinguishable from sexuality and/or fetish ? can it be just an style or aesthetic ? sure, but 1. there are multiple styles and aesthetics within furry itself and 2. i\u2019m incredibly wary of pushes to separate or obscure or just plain hide or dismiss sexuality in furry after previous history engaging with it, or reading a lot of the history involving it, especially w/r/t how it treated LGBT folx in furry.<br /> i was saying the other day that people tend to view furry as an all in or all out binary, but considering the amount of people who have cranked it to lola bunny, or drawn talking animal people comics of their own, without having idea one of furry as a community or art at all, this isn\u2019t the case. people who\u2019ve never even so much of heard of furaffinity have made furry material, or had furry sexual fantasies. sexual or not, the concept is awfully broad. ancient, even. remember that post about one of the oldest pieces of art being a small figurine of a human with an animal head?<br /> the worry about sexuality, the anxiety over \u201coooooh how should we distinguish between non-sexual and sexual furry material ooooh it\u2019s terribly important for respectability reasons\u201d and all that kinda stuff, comes off as incredibly misguided to me, especially at a time when it\u2019s mainstreaming at a wild pace.<br /> so, like, yeah, you can make completely sexuality free furry stuff, be totally into sexuality free furry stuff, but the want to do so as a sort of active opposition to or resistance to sexuality in furry is just\u2026 it\u2019s not great. sci-fi fans don\u2019t worry half this much about material featuring fucking aliens, including not particularly human ones like garrus, who is WILDLY fucking popular. the disgust or resentment, the anxiety and worry of sexuality in furry, is what comes off as incredibly suspect to me. especially when people were making sexually charged furry material before \u201cfurry\u201d as a community existed.<br /> in short: if you wanna do furry stuff that\u2019s completely non-sexual, that\u2019s your bag, then go for it, absolutely. just don\u2019t stress or get all weird about the people who do like it sexual. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T05:30:27-07:00","id":971266,"title":"","content":"Lately, me and my friends has started to play Iron Claw. While I've never was into &quot;furrys&quot; (I've never felt like it was serious enough), the first session actually went ok, and didn't felt weird or silly. I've even decided to totally get out of my comfort zone and play a female character (a jackal called Alberta), something which I've never done, and it was quit enjoyable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T15:05:11-07:00","id":971530,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/968396-the-furry-thread?p=971266#post971266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lately, me and my friends has started to play Iron Claw. While I've never was into &amp;quot;furrys&amp;quot; (I've never felt like it was serious enough), the first session actually went ok, and didn't felt weird or silly. I've even decided to totally get out of my comfort zone and play a female character (a jackal called Alberta), something which I've never done, and it was quit enjoyable.</div> </div> </div> </div>There was a recent Kickstarter for an Ironclaw expansion that adds the setting's equivalent of North Africa and the Middle East that looked super neat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T22:53:37-07:00","id":971780,"title":"","content":"I'll check it out, thanks :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T23:09:27-07:00","id":971782,"title":"","content":"I'm not gonna lie, given how many furry Changeling players I've personally known and how popular both Werewolf games are, I'm a little stunned how quiet this thread has been.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T00:51:00-07:00","id":971812,"title":"","content":"I've always considered myself a furry, but I've never really engaged much with the larger furry community. It's not that I don't want to, as much as I have difficulty insinuating myself into pretty much any social group. Still, I've always felt insulted myself whenever I've seen anyone talking shit about other furries.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksi plays Peek-a-boo for keeps. ~ nalak42","edited":{"userid":203,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/203-kleptomania","user":"Kleptomania","date":". 09-18-2016, 03:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/203-kleptomania","name":"Kleptomania","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar203_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T00:58:40-07:00","id":971815,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kleptomania</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/968396-the-furry-thread?p=971812#post971812\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've always considered myself a furry, but I've never really engaged much with the larger furry community. It's not that I don't want to, as much as I have difficulty insinuating myself into pretty much any social group. Still, I've always felt insulted myself whenever I've seen anyone talking shit about other furries.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you have any characters of your own?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T01:34:42-07:00","id":971832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/968396-the-furry-thread?p=971815#post971815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Do you have any characters of your own?</div> </div> </div> </div>I've had a number over the years, but I'm not sure if I currently consider any my personal 'fursona'.<br /> <br /> The one I've liked the most was a fun-loving and optimistic bull, usually going by 'Bright' who stands out as the opposite of my usually glum self. I occasionally role-played him with the few furry friends I have, but I always was a little awkward with it.<br /> Another was an exceedingly cynical lizard with a severe case of wanderlust, who I've used as inspiration for several characters in various things. In his original incarnation though, I always envisioned him dressing like some bizarre sort of greaser. I never decided on a lasting name for him.<br /> One of my first characters was a lion who I can't quite remember the name of, just that he mostly mirrored my own personality.<br /> There were others, but they weren't so notable to me.<br /> <br /> I always kind of wanted to commission someone to draw one of my characters, but never really did. I briefly tried to draw Bright myself, but my art skills are pretty terrible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksi plays Peek-a-boo for keeps. ~ nalak42","edited":{"userid":203,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/203-kleptomania","user":"Kleptomania","date":". 09-18-2016, 08:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/203-kleptomania","name":"Kleptomania","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar203_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T06:34:49-07:00","id":971904,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/968396-the-furry-thread?p=971782#post971782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not gonna lie, given how many furry Changeling players I've personally known and how popular both Werewolf games are, I'm a little stunned how quiet this thread has been.</div> </div> </div> </div>Both Werewolf games have a &quot;furry&quot; form that is far from neutral in its range of activities. You go into Crinos and Gauru only if you're expecting a fight, because they're going to make any other activity difficult, what with the likelihood of flying off the handle and the non-negotiable Appearance of 0 and all (even Kitsune in W:tA have Appearance 0 to normal humans in Koto form). The Delirium/Lunacy and the long-ago actions of Garou culling humans might also play into this, since the Garou and Uratha are literally ragemonsters so scary that humans don't want to believe that they exist. It's sort of like how I've heard that the majority of furries in Exalted don't play Lunars, they play Solars or other non-Lunar Exalted, and make them beastfolk.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T16:41:24-07:00","id":972202,"title":"","content":"As a zealous werewolf fan I will also point out that, while werewolves have fur, being a fan of the game doesn't mean you have any interest in the furry community or are a furry.<br /> <br /> I may be wrong, but there do seem to be some furries in the werewolf forum. It's possible they just don't look at the Off-Topic threads.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T17:22:23-07:00","id":972224,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/968396-the-furry-thread?p=972202#post972202\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a zealous werewolf fan I will also point out that, while werewolves have fur, being a fan of the game doesn't mean you have any interest in the furry community or are a furry.<br /> <br /> I may be wrong, but there do seem to be some furries in the werewolf forum. It's possible they just don't look at the Off-Topic threads.</div> </div> </div> </div>In my experience, I have run into a few Apocalypse fans who are largely into the game in order to have in-character sex at LARPs. While I doubt that's anything resembling more than a fraction of a percentile of the community, those folks make me laugh whenever I laugh at them.<br /> <br /> And I think the arguments you occasionally see about &quot;why can't I walk around in war form?&quot; for either game speak to some sort of furry tendency.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":281,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","user":"atamajakki","date":". 09-18-2016, 08:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T17:39:33-07:00","id":972231,"title":"","content":"I'll echo nofather. I'm a big fan of WtA and have played in Werewolf LARPS and TT for over ten years, and none of the gamers I've played with(around a dozen or so) were Furries. I've definitely run across a few at comic book conventions and such. At least, I think they were.<br /> <br /> To each his/her own.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":95,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","user":"Fat Larry","date":". 09-18-2016, 10:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T18:24:36-07:00","id":972252,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/968396-the-furry-thread?p=972224#post972224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In my experience, I have run into a few Apocalypse fans who are largely into the game in order to have in-character sex at LARPs. While I doubt that's anything resembling more than a fraction of a percentile of the community, those folks make me laugh whenever I laugh at them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I couldn't say if that means they're furry or not, and I've never been involved with a LARP.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And I think the arguments you occasionally see about &quot;why can't I walk around in war form?&quot; for either game speak to some sort of furry tendency. </div> </div> </div>Yes, this and the frequent requests for Changing Breeds that involve other were-variants is what makes me think that there are furries who enjoy the game. But it's entirely possible they want to for other reasons.<br /> <br /> In regards to your original question, <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Does anyone else here have experiences with the whole furry phenomenon, or have any characters they'd like to share? </div> </div> </div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">as someone who's been around the internet since the early 90s while the furry phenomenon certainly seemed to take a lot of hits, especially as it became less acceptable to mock other groups, they seem like they've survived and thrived, even if there's still a lot of people who find it unbearable for other people to enjoy. Online, at least. I don't believe I've ever encountered it in person, outside of the odd girl wearing cat ears or a tail.</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 09-18-2016, 09:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T18:53:20-07:00","id":972264,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/968396-the-furry-thread?p=972252#post972252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">as someone who's been around the internet since the early 90s while the furry phenomenon certainly seemed to take a lot of hits, especially as it became less acceptable to mock other groups, they seem like they've survived and thrived, even if there's still a lot of people who find it unbearable for other people to enjoy. Online, at least. I don't believe I've ever encountered it in person, outside of the odd girl wearing cat ears or a tail.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>The timeline I shared in the OP is appropriately named <i>Everyone's a Furry 2k16</i>, and that's honestly how it's kind of seemed as the past few years have gone on. Especially on Tumblr, I'm seeing a lot of folks whose art started out furry and now they're publicly revisiting it due to the bandwagoning hate dying down or people like me who use it as another layer of a larger queer identity; there's been an explosion of people with explicitly trans on nonbinary fursonas now, and it's great to see. That's before how popular Zootopia turned out to be, but Disney always gets a sort of pass on being furry to the wider public.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T20:28:23-07:00","id":972306,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/968396-the-furry-thread?p=972224#post972224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In my experience, I have run into a few Apocalypse fans who are largely into the game in order to have in-character sex at LARPs. While I doubt that's anything resembling more than a fraction of a percentile of the community, those folks make me laugh whenever I laugh at them.</div> </div> </div> </div>A lot of people are into <i>LARPing</i> in order to have in-character sex at LARPs. Werewolf is one of the worst genres for in-character sex because it's VERBOTEN.<br /> <br /> Sarcasm: Fera players, though? Furverts, the lot of them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T20:38:59-07:00","id":972312,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>etherial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/968396-the-furry-thread?p=972306#post972306\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A lot of people are into <i>LARPing</i> in order to have in-character sex at LARPs. Werewolf is one of the worst genres for in-character sex because it's VERBOTEN.<br /> <br /> Sarcasm: Fera players, though? Furverts, the lot of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, because taboo always stops people from having sex, right? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T01:03:07-07:00","id":972387,"title":"","content":"Not every furry needs to be in a relationship with another furry to find it sexually fulfilling. I feel like that's something that's often missed. Of my furry friends, a good number are in happy long term relationships with people that don't identify as furry.<br /> <br /> And I've seen a lot of people play kinfolk just for the sexy times aspect of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T01:20:37-07:00","id":972394,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/968396-the-furry-thread?p=972387#post972387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not every furry needs to be in a relationship with another furry to find it sexually fulfilling. I feel like that's something that's often missed. Of my furry friends, a good number are in happy long term relationships with people that don't identify as furry.<br /> <br /> And I've seen a lot of people play kinfolk just for the sexy times aspect of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, my significant other has nothing to do with the furry scene and was honestly afraid of it until super recently.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T06:56:31-07:00","id":972491,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/968396-the-furry-thread#post968396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does anyone else here have experiences with the whole furry phenomenon, or have any characters they'd like to share? I'd obviously prefer this not become a gigantic dump of porn, bad art, and fetish sex stories, but things will probably take a mature turn. I'm curious to see where this winds up!</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm in it. I've no artistic talent, but enjoy supporting artists when I can. I've gotten commissions, been to a few conventions and met a few people about in the fandom that are genuinely cool people. <br /> <br /> Werewolf:the Apocalypse was one of my first outlets for Furry. Though I've had fun with Ironclaw before as well. One of the things that Beast: the Primordial really amuses me with is how literal you can make the statement &quot;Fuck you, I'm a dragon&quot; with a flamethrower impression.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T08:52:48-07:00","id":974438,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/968396-the-furry-thread?p=972312#post972312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, because taboo always stops people from having sex, right? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Well, after a certain point if they catch you doing it, yes. Violations of the first tenet are grounds for execution or exile in many caerns, and exile for Garou is often as good as being executed because of how their enemies will single out a lone werewolf for lethal payback. With Fera, it's not always a guarantee to be taboo, though. In fact, Nagah have to sustain their numbers that way in many cases, because they're a Super Secret Splat that's not supposed to be alive anymore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T11:56:29-07:00","id":974569,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/968396-the-furry-thread?p=974438#post974438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, after a certain point if they catch you doing it, yes. Violations of the first tenet are grounds for execution or exile in many caerns, and exile for Garou is often as good as being executed because of how their enemies will single out a lone werewolf for lethal payback.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exile is just tempting them to Fall. Best to load them up with ammo and throw them at a Thunderwyrm. If they succeed, you welcome them back. If they fail, they died gloriously for Gaia.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T16:26:08-07:00","id":974730,"title":"","content":"Well forsaken werewolves don't have that problem, though the lack of LARP rules and having to get a particular gift to do so are minor annoyances.<br /> <br /> As for furries in the WtA fandom, I found a fur affinity page for Vermiis, the guy whose BSD character got elected to the Pentax board, and it seems there are a lot of BSD furry characters in general on the internet based on my look at it so I am guessing the BSDs have some sort of appeal that I can't get.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":3932,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","user":"The young man in the cafe","date":". 09-22-2016, 07:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T06:25:26-07:00","id":975023,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The young man in the cafe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/968396-the-furry-thread?p=974730#post974730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">it seems there are a lot of BSD furry characters in general on the internet based on my look at it so I am guessing the BSDs have some sort of appeal that I can't get.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Probably because 90s WW was obsessed with BDSM BSDs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T07:55:27-07:00","id":975050,"title":"","content":"Y'know, going into this thread, I didn't think I had anything to do with Furryism. But thinking back on it...<br /> <br /> I've been into animal characters since I was a kid, coming up with OCs for things like Watership Down and crossing over The Rescuers with NIMH...and don't even get me started on Redwall! Later on I got into Fred Perry's Gold Digger, and I'm no stranger to his more risque Furry stories. When I got into WW, I admit that I probably made more Pooka characters than any other Changeling type, but I never really saw Werewolf as being &quot;Furry&quot;...but now that I think about it, however, the guys I played with in college basically threw out most of the games' canon setting so that they could play lighthearted &quot;League of Super-Fera&quot; stories...<br /> <br /> But I was never really into the overall community. I've never even heard the term &quot;fursona&quot; before this thread, for example! The closest I come to that is that I used to be really into Astrology, but being very introverted, I don't match my Leo sign at all (stupid Scorpio Ascendant...!), so I used to symbolize that as me being a Black Panther, not unlike the Marvel Mangaverse version (art obviously not by me):<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://static8.comicvine.com/uploads/scale_small/1/15776/637720-blackpanther1.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>]<br /> <br /> ...Shit, maybe I <i>am</i> a Furry.<br /> <br /> Does being a Pony fan count? There seems to be three different variants to Pony fan-art/fiction, basic Ponies, Humanized Ponies, and Anthros, which are somewhere in between. I would definitely count the Anthro-fans as Furries, but not sure about the rest...Anyway, I've really drifted away from the above over the years, aside from being a Pony fan (tho not a transgender one, despite my avatar!<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />) <br /> <br /> I hope this thread doesn't awaken something within me! <span style=\"font-size:10px\">(Community reference, for those who haven't seen the show!)</span><br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T07:59:40-07:00","id":975053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>etherial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/968396-the-furry-thread?p=972306#post972306\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A lot of people are into <i>LARPing</i> in order to have in-character sex at LARPs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait, roleplaying that actually <i>gets </i>you laid?! What is this, topsy-turvy day?<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Just remembered, btw, that I do have a friend into the scene, who even posts pics of himself in costume at conventions on his Facebook page. My other friends have raised eyebrows at this, but basically have gotten used to it, and so make no further comment on it. <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T09:42:56-07:00","id":975099,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/968396-the-furry-thread?p=975053#post975053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait, roleplaying that actually <i>gets </i>you laid?! What is this, topsy-turvy day?<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>IC sex and OOC sex are a venn diagram.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T11:52:44-07:00","id":975149,"title":"","content":"I've scribbled up ideas for some additional characters past my fursona who populate her setting: her best friend Hermes (a squirrel, bike courier, and fellow food truck nerd) and her coworker Heruka (a bright red tiger who may or may not have three eyes, focuses on Southeast Asian antiques, and martial arts fanboy). A friend of mine recently told me she's looking at an okapi fursona for herself, which may well be the cutest thing I've ever heard.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T15:03:45-07:00","id":975245,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/968396-the-furry-thread?p=975053#post975053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wait, roleplaying that actually <i>gets </i>you laid?! What is this, topsy-turvy day?<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Just remembered, btw, that I do have a friend into the scene, who even posts pics of himself in costume at conventions on his Facebook page. My other friends have raised eyebrows at this, but basically have gotten used to it, and so make no further comment on it. <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>When I attended the FurAffinity: United convention when it moved to its new hotel in northern Virginia this year, I got asked by three separate people at the bar what was going on. There was mostly confusion, curiosity and amusement. And when I told the guy who was trying to take sneaky pictures of the fursuiters that if he asked them if he could take a picture, they'd probably pose for him, I started to get a lot of questions. <br /> <br /> Wasnt a bad experience honestly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T16:25:01-07:00","id":975265,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The young man in the cafe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/968396-the-furry-thread?p=974730#post974730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am guessing the BSDs have some sort of appeal that I can't get.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't knock it till you try it.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T22:47:09-07:00","id":975380,"title":"","content":"Guess who just bought new art!<br /> <br /> Slightly nsfw (it's a tasteful nude, not smut or anything), but I love how it came out: <a href=\"http://sunflowerbun.tumblr.com/post/150843590406/sexy-moo-commission-for-atamajakki\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T23:06:23-07:00","id":975387,"title":"","content":"Nice. It reminds me of Hator somehow","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T23:11:13-07:00","id":975388,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/968396-the-furry-thread?p=975387#post975387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nice. It reminds me of Hator somehow</div> </div> </div> </div>Hah, I mentioned Hathor when I reuploaded it to furaffinity! Keftiu has heavy inspiration from both Hathor and Apis, though she originally sprang from a fringe Scion or Unknown Armies character concept around reinventing the Azar/Osiris myth as a transgender woman narrative (i.e. abandon masculinity to become god of the underworld), and her name is the Egyptian word for the Minoans. Keftiu is very, very much steeped in Egyptian goddess symbolism by design.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T15:41:49-07:00","id":975716,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/968396-the-furry-thread?p=971160#post971160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not gonna deny that a fairly massive chunk of the art out there is pornographic, but I'm also not sure that has to be a bad thing. The awesome person, Spacetwinks, behind the timeline in my OP had this to say in response to a later question about it, which nicely handles things; in other words, the talk shouldn't be &quot;not all furry stuff is porn!&quot; but rather &quot;why is it bad if so much of it is?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I think there's elements of transphobia and homophobia which have a lot to do with the negative association of sexuality with furries, and that people attempting to distance their own non-sexual content from the sexual content are often engaged in respectability politics because they feel that their interests are unfairly marginalized by association. Ideally we all understand that this is not a good thing that people feel the need to defend themselves from that kind of stigma, but y'know how people can be.<br /> <br /> I also think there's also a small discomfort with the potential association that furry has with bestiality, <i>and</i> there's the awkward intersection of that stigma with marginalized sexual and gender identities too that turns it into a quagmire that's not easily resolved for people both people on the outside and for those who are within that community.<br /> <br /> By this I mean marginalized sexualities and gender identities get associated with &quot;deviancy&quot; and deviancy is associated with bestiality. It's how you get people like Professors at acclaimed private institutions writing that allowing gay marriage opens the door for necrophilia, bestiality et al. On top of that, you get the more straightforward association of animals as a component of furries and bestiality, and you have an interest group (furries) which gets associated with deviancy both by virtue of base subject matter and by associating with actual marginalized identity. That's very likely where you get continuous discomfort with the notion of furries outside of those groups which are furries or hate them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":159,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","user":"Leetsepeak","date":". 09-25-2016, 02:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T22:56:24-07:00","id":975840,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"159\" data-vbnamecard=\"159\">Leetsepeak</a> I think a lot of that is valid, yeah. One of the explanations I've seen for a lot of the anti-furry vitriol out there (beyond what's expected from some of the more unfortunate members of the fandom being altogether too public about some things) is that so much furry content has been shamelessly queer, even well before the internet but certainly in the last decade or so, and that the nascent alt-right latched onto the &quot;yiff in hell&quot; bandwagon at least in part due to the large amount of queer stuff in the mix. There's gay slice-of-life romances from the 90s that saw decent readership, and going after the weird animal people is an easy smokescreen for being upset with LGBT characters. While there's still a ton of gross fetishization of transgender characters within furry art, there's also a massive amount of more inoffensive and tasteful work that's exploded out in the last few years.<br /> <br /> And to lighten the mood somewhat, another <a href=\"http://d.facdn.net/art/fubbawubba/1474779806/1474779806.fubbawubba_chib2__2_.png\" target=\"_blank\">new piece of art</a>!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T06:02:29-07:00","id":975919,"title":"","content":"Can't see it for some reason. Only a blank &quot;forbidden&quot; page.","sign