px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"https://67.media.tumblr.com/0ffee8159c0bef607e3b78aef793fba1/tumblr_oe1njoGZ0I1r21rsxo1_540.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T13:08:30-07:00","id":976063,"title":"","content":"Cool! Thanks. Maybe you can use that as your avatar too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T20:31:23-07:00","id":976914,"title":"","content":"In high school I experimented a bit with furry. Had a bear character, don't remember their name and never had any art done up of them. Played around with straight and gay sex, and some transgender (the character was both male and female). That persisted a little into college but for the most part I moved on. I realize now that it was an early way for me to experiment with my sexuality in an extra-anonymous fashion even though at this point I'm confidently cisgender and mostly heterosexual.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T19:11:04-07:00","id":978131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/968396-the-furry-thread?p=971782#post971782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not gonna lie, given how many furry Changeling players I've personally known and how popular both Werewolf games are, I'm a little stunned how quiet this thread has been.</div> </div> </div> </div>Im both into W:tA and Furry fandom.<br /> <br /> I think there is a lot the RPG group can learn from the furrys! First, if White wolf is looking for the self sustain community, the furry fandom is the perfect example.<br /> <br /> The moment you step in the furry fandom, people ask for your Fursona, what I learned is this.<br /> <br /> 1) In the furry fandom it's very important have a visual representation of your Fursona, that attracts a lot of artists offering commission. On top of that, all furry content is created by yourself.<br /> Furry Artists have No Fear of making art, unlike you doing a Fan art, and have risk of be sued or your art removed. Furrys are the creator of their own content, not consumers.<br /> <br /> White wolf still very vague about User Generated Content as show here 19min17seg<br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://youtu.be/p9ezN0vwKhA?t=19m17s\" data-code=\"p9ezN0vwKhA\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/p9ezN0vwKhA/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> But I hope, if they do it right, a lot of werewolf artists that migrates to the furry fandom will come back into W:tA.<br /> Unless I'm wrong and rpg player dont care about make art of they character...<br /> <br /> 2) In the furry fandom, mostly of the times, the fursona is a better version of yourself. Unlike in World of Darkness, that explore the dark side of yourself. Furrys generally have 1 fursona at time, and at a very long time, almost for life some times.<br /> So, furrys can proudly say this fursona is me, but a little better, I'm proud of it.<br /> <br /> The World of Darkness explore the dark side but the player in general are mature adults and understand what is fantasy, but still, I dont think vampires are a better version of yourself, it's a messy version in a quest to make ourselves better. Not sure player here identify that much with one character as a furry do with his fursona, this could be discussion for a new topic.<br /> <br /> 3) The most important, and I think this goes for both communities, what furrys are really looking for is not sex, they are looking for a place to belong, the desire of human connection. It sad me the other communities could learn a lot from furrys and I believe we all here RPG player are not just looking for numbers in your character sheet, but for meaningful connection with people...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11329,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11329-neowuf","user":"Neowuf","date":". 09-28-2016, 10:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11329-neowuf","name":"Neowuf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11329_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T21:04:24-07:00","id":978177,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neowuf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/968396-the-furry-thread?p=978131#post978131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2) In the furry fandom, mostly of the times, the fursona is a better version of yourself. Unlike in World of Darkness, that explore the dark side of yourself. Furrys generally have 1 fursona at time, and at a very long time, almost for life some times.<br /> So, furrys can proudly say this fursona is me, but a little better, I'm proud of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>This has definitely jumped out at me recently. I'm questioning my own gender and in a place where I'm not safe to experiment with how I present, so having a fursona who is trans, sure of it, safely out, and passing has been a lovely vent for my angst. That she happens to have a cute history-related job and eats a lot of food truck food is just incidental, I'm sure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T21:53:39-07:00","id":978202,"title":"","content":"My relationship with the furry fandom is a bit complicated. On the one hand I'm adamantly a transhumanist. If it ever becomes possible I intend to upload in a heartbeat, and if/when that happens I see no reason to just be human, though I don't really see myself taking on an anthropomorphic identity or what have you. I grew up on stories like the Firebringer Trilogy, so that's more my speed.<br /> <br /> As for the fandom itself? My issue isn't that so much furry art is porn, it's that so much of it is 'bad' porn. I do think there is that distinction. Often the proportions just aren't realistic, the artists' biases show through regarding sex, gender, the roles for them, etc. I'm also transgender, so it doesn't make me uncomfortable at all when I see stuff depicting transformations in a purely fetish light, often done by people who just have a fetish for some kind of helplessness or lack of control. I can filter these, and I do when I bother searching sites like Fur Affinity, but it does make it so I've never fully committed to the community. That said, I think there are some really great artists out there, and if it helps people express themselves then so much the better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T02:29:42-07:00","id":978287,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/968396-the-furry-thread?p=978202#post978202\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My relationship with the furry fandom is a bit complicated. On the one hand I'm adamantly a transhumanist. If it ever becomes possible I intend to upload in a heartbeat, and if/when that happens I see no reason to just be human, though I don't really see myself taking on an anthropomorphic identity or what have you. I grew up on stories like the Firebringer Trilogy, so that's more my speed.<br /> <br /> As for the fandom itself? My issue isn't that so much furry art is porn, it's that so much of it is 'bad' porn. I do think there is that distinction. Often the proportions just aren't realistic, the artists' biases show through regarding sex, gender, the roles for them, etc. I'm also transgender, so it doesn't make me uncomfortable at all when I see stuff depicting transformations in a purely fetish light, often done by people who just have a fetish for some kind of helplessness or lack of control. I can filter these, and I do when I bother searching sites like Fur Affinity, but it does make it so I've never fully committed to the community. That said, I think there are some really great artists out there, and if it helps people express themselves then so much the better.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's thankfully been a pretty big push from a lot of younger artists to reclaim a lot of the queer content with furry art, giving us a lot of more believable trans characters as opposed to the old gross slur-ridden mainstays you still see a lot of. Things are much more body-positive and less fetishized than they've ever been before, and that seems to only be gaining more momentum. While there's still an ocean of awful and offensive stuff to wade through, that's true of pretty much any large community. I'm glad furry stuff seems to be cleaning up its act in some small ways.<br /> <br /> As an aside, I'd love to chat you up about transhumanist stuff sometime!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":281,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","user":"atamajakki","date":". 09-29-2016, 05:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T01:56:40-07:00","id":978928,"title":"","content":"I've considered experimenting and becoming involved in the furry scene, but I'm kind of worried about the social stigma attached to it. I mean no offense, I just am very self-conscious and I worry a lot about how others perceive me, mainly due to bad experiences as an adolescent that were partly my fault and partly the fault of high schoolers being complete assholes.<br /> <br /> \u200bIf I did have a fursona, I'd probably be a wolf. I know it's overdone, but I'm thinking just a plain gray wolf (perhaps a dire wolf, since dire wolves were huge and I was always the tallest person in my social circles. I'm over six and a half feet tall and have a stocky build), nothing too fancy like bright colors or wings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T02:29:44-07:00","id":978931,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Camilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/968396-the-furry-thread?p=978928#post978928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've considered experimenting and becoming involved in the furry scene, but I'm kind of worried about the social stigma attached to it. I mean no offense, I just am very self-conscious and I worry a lot about how others perceive me, mainly due to bad experiences as an adolescent that were partly my fault and partly the fault of high schoolers being complete assholes.<br /> <br /> \u200bIf I did have a fursona, I'd probably be a wolf. I know it's overdone, but I'm thinking just a plain gray wolf (perhaps a dire wolf, since dire wolves were huge and I was always the tallest person in my social circles. I'm over six and a half feet tall and have a stocky build), nothing too fancy like bright colors or wings.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, I don't do anything other than talk to a handful of furry friends (who I know through other things primarily) and then buy art for my own enjoyment. You don't have to get involved in any way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T03:07:03-07:00","id":978939,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/968396-the-furry-thread?p=978931#post978931\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean, I don't do anything other than talk to a handful of furry friends (who I know through other things primarily) and then buy art for my own enjoyment. You don't have to get involved in any way.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bThing is, I do want to get involved on a certain level. Most of the furries I know IRL are friends I know through other interests as well. I do like the idea of having a fursona and I think it would be cool. Plus, I think this furry thing could help me experiment and work through some issues of mine also.<br /> <br /> \u200batamajakki, I have some questions and other personal issues I wish to discuss, mind if I send you a PM?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T08:43:16-07:00","id":979062,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Camilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/968396-the-furry-thread?p=978939#post978939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bThing is, I do want to get involved on a certain level. Most of the furries I know IRL are friends I know through other interests as well. I do like the idea of having a fursona and I think it would be cool. Plus, I think this furry thing could help me experiment and work through some issues of mine also.<br /> <br /> \u200batamajakki, I have some questions and other personal issues I wish to discuss, mind if I send you a PM?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> There's nothing inherently wrong with being a furry, though there are some groups/individuals who can give it a bad name. That's true of basically any label you might use to identify yourself with, though. Get out there, expand your own identity, and make some friends I say.<br /> <br /> And if you run into people who dismiss you over a label instead of taking the time to get to know you, or have friends who distance themselves from you after exploring that, then they weren't really friendship material. People who are only friends with you because you play a role to suit them aren't friends at all in my mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T08:51:51-07:00","id":979075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/968396-the-furry-thread?p=979062#post979062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> There's nothing inherently wrong with being a furry, though there are some groups/individuals who can give it a bad name. That's true of basically any label you might use to identify yourself with, though. Get out there, expand your own identity, and make some friends I say.<br /> <br /> And if you run into people who dismiss you over a label instead of taking the time to get to know you, or have friends who distance themselves from you after exploring that, then they weren't really friendship material. People who are only friends with you because you play a role to suit them aren't friends at all in my mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bThank you for your support. I think will explore this newfound interest in furry, and I even have found a name for my fursona. Samuel, a gray dire wolf.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T11:04:42-07:00","id":979158,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Camilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/968396-the-furry-thread?p=978939#post978939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bThing is, I do want to get involved on a certain level. Most of the furries I know IRL are friends I know through other interests as well. I do like the idea of having a fursona and I think it would be cool. Plus, I think this furry thing could help me experiment and work through some issues of mine also.<br /> <br /> \u200batamajakki, I have some questions and other personal issues I wish to discuss, mind if I send you a PM?</div> </div> </div> </div>Feel free to hit me up~","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T12:02:00-07:00","id":979182,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/968396-the-furry-thread?p=979158#post979158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Feel free to hit me up~</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI just sent you a PM.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T19:27:27-07:00","id":980009,"title":"","content":"Correct me if I'm way off base (and many apologies if I offend), but is there some psychological or thematic overlap with the Otherkin community and the Fur community? I'm thinking of a few things that seem like personal gray areas on this subject, when analyzing myself under a furred lens.<br /> <br /> Many thanks for any response!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T20:11:42-07:00","id":980030,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AzraelFirestorm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/968396-the-furry-thread?p=980009#post980009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Correct me if I'm way off base (and many apologies if I offend), but is there some psychological or thematic overlap with the Otherkin community and the Fur community? I'm thinking of a few things that seem like personal gray areas on this subject, when analyzing myself under a furred lens.<br /> <br /> Many thanks for any response!</div> </div> </div> </div>There's definitely some overlap there, but it would be a mistake to assume the average furry and the average otherkin or therian have a whole lot in common. I know some of folks who are both - and one uses her fursona as a way to have some sort of outlet for her feline self - but the vast majority are not, and there's a lot of otherkin scorn in and outside of furries. I definitely have nothing in common with any otherkin, as my character is purely an animal out of an aesthetic choice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T18:02:04-07:00","id":981148,"title":"","content":"I'm in a weird place where I want to buy NSFW artwork (not out-and-out porn, but a little more than a tasteful nude) of my character but don't want to contribute to the gross fetishization of trans women and feel a little bashful about this thing that's basically /me/ being out there and sexual. All these reservations feel overwhelming, but at the same time I pretty much don't get to feel attractive or erotic in my actual life so letting this representation of myself have that is lovely, but then we circle back around to the above thoughts and I get stuck in a loop.<br /> <br /> Ugh.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T18:13:51-07:00","id":981153,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/968396-the-furry-thread?p=981148#post981148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm in a weird place where I want to buy NSFW artwork (not out-and-out porn, but a little more than a tasteful nude) of my character but don't want to contribute to the gross fetishization of trans women and feel a little bashful about this thing that's basically /me/ being out there and sexual. All these reservations feel overwhelming, but at the same time I pretty much don't get to feel attractive or erotic in my actual life so letting this representation of myself have that is lovely, but then we circle back around to the above thoughts and I get stuck in a loop.<br /> <br /> Ugh.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <a href=\"http://www.furaffinity.net/user/drpickelle/\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.furaffinity.net/user/drpickelle/</a> Seems pretty good for sensual art that isn't sex. Good luck getting a commission though, by the looks of it.<br /> <br /> You could also commission something and then request that the artist not make it public?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T18:23:53-07:00","id":981156,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/968396-the-furry-thread?p=981153#post981153\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.furaffinity.net/user/drpickelle/\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.furaffinity.net/user/drpickelle/</a> Seems pretty good for sensual art that isn't sex. Good luck getting a commission though, by the looks of it.<br /> <br /> You could also commission something and then request that the artist not make it public?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, it's less that and more... wanting to get it right, I guess? This character is my only real outlet for both my gender identity and my feeling desirable, so I'm putting wholly too much thought and emotional stake into what is ultimately a pretty drawing of an animal person.<br /> <br /> I really want to buy from <a href=\"https://www.furaffinity.net/user/deckland/\" target=\"_blank\">www.furaffinity.net/user/deckland/</a> again, and then <a href=\"https://www.furaffinity.net/user/oouna/\" target=\"_blank\">www.furaffinity.net/user/oouna/</a> is my unlikely &quot;when will I ever have have a spare $200&quot; dream artist. Both are really good at sensual, respectful stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T18:47:12-07:00","id":981175,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/968396-the-furry-thread?p=981156#post981156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah, it's less that and more... wanting to get it right, I guess?</div> </div> </div> </div>I personally would feel really embarrassed sharing that aspect of myself with a person I'm not familiar with, I can well imagine that feeling that said person might not be able to capture just what you mean.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/968396-the-furry-thread?p=981156#post981156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This character is my only real outlet for both my gender identity and my feeling desirable, so I'm putting wholly too much thought and emotional stake into what is ultimately a pretty drawing of an animal person.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds like it's bit more than just a pretty drawing. In general I get the impression that if furries 'could' be their fursona, like in a hypothetical transhumanism society where people could just upload their brains onto computers, most of them would 'look' like their fursonas. That effectively makes it a pretty strong identity signifier, and I'm not really in the habit of trivializing people over their identity. If you're capable of using it as a prop to swear a Changeling the Lost Fae Oath then it seems pretty serious to me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/968396-the-furry-thread?p=981156#post981156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really want to buy from <a href=\"https://www.furaffinity.net/user/deckland/\" target=\"_blank\">www.furaffinity.net/user/deckland/</a> again, and then <a href=\"https://www.furaffinity.net/user/oouna/\" target=\"_blank\">www.furaffinity.net/user/oouna/</a> is my unlikely &quot;when will I ever have have a spare $200&quot; dream artist. Both are really good at sensual, respectful stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>Those are pretty cool, but I'd have to come up with a fursona, and man I work like 60 hours a week and still don't have money for anything. : \\","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T19:08:45-07:00","id":981195,"title":"","content":"Been involved in the fandom for about 15 years now and got to know a lot of wonderful people despite never meeting and of them in person. Very welcoming community!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1666-firstborn8","name":"Firstborn8","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T19:55:35-07:00","id":981223,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/968396-the-furry-thread?p=981175#post981175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I personally would feel really embarrassed sharing that aspect of myself with a person I'm not familiar with, I can well imagine that feeling that said person might not be able to capture just what you mean.</div> </div> </div> </div> I don't much care if anyone sees art of my character, but I definitely don't want to do what so many others do and just purchase a mountain of tasteless porn with her and strangers' characters. She's me, damn it! That means something!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/968396-the-furry-thread?p=981175#post981175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sounds like it's bit more than just a pretty drawing. In general I get the impression that if furries 'could' be their fursona, like in a hypothetical transhumanism society where people could just upload their brains onto computers, most of them would 'look' like their fursonas. That effectively makes it a pretty strong identity signifier, and I'm not really in the habit of trivializing people over their identity. If you're capable of using it as a prop to swear a Changeling the Lost Fae Oath then it seems pretty serious to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't you know us evil SJWs hate all personal identity and want to take it away from everyone else? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> But yeah, I've spent so much time in transhuman circles out of a deep-seated wish to change how I look, and I definitely think furry plays into that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/968396-the-furry-thread?p=981175#post981175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Those are pretty cool, but I'd have to come up with a fursona, and man I work like 60 hours a week and still don't have money for anything. : \\</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd been kind of passively a fan of furry art for about a decade now, but it's only super recently (probably about four months back?) with the realization that I'm probably trans and don't have a safe outlet to explore that currently that led to me finally creating a fursona. Take your zodiac sign and smash it together with a lot of Egyptian mythology and the clothes you wish you could wear; that's all I did. Even with tipping super generously, most of the art I've bought has cost under $50, and even my full ref sheet plus tip was under $100.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T23:23:23-07:00","id":981288,"title":"","content":"Ah, so you are a Taurus? That explains the cow thing. Nice, nice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T09:18:01-07:00","id":981483,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/968396-the-furry-thread?p=981148#post981148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm in a weird place where I want to buy NSFW artwork (not out-and-out porn, but a little more than a tasteful nude) of my character but don't want to contribute to the gross fetishization of trans women and feel a little bashful about this thing that's basically /me/ being out there and sexual. All these reservations feel overwhelming, but at the same time I pretty much don't get to feel attractive or erotic in my actual life so letting this representation of myself have that is lovely, but then we circle back around to the above thoughts and I get stuck in a loop.<br /> <br /> Ugh.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've spent a bit on commissions myself and if you'd like a little advice on getting what you want out of a commission, feel free to hit me up on that.<br /> <br /> Also, a number of the artists I've interacted with mostly draw the &quot;out-and-out porn&quot; stuff because it sells and it's what commissioners have been commissioning them for, but I've had some artists who draw some of that be very happy to get a commissioner who specifically wants something &quot;tasteful&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T10:25:30-07:00","id":981506,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/968396-the-furry-thread?p=981288#post981288\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah, so you are a Taurus? That explains the cow thing. Nice, nice.</div> </div> </div> </div>One part Taurus, one part Egyptian cow deities (Hathor, the goddess of women and love, and Apis, the divine sacrificial bull), one part the archaic &quot;cow-eyed/ox-eyed&quot; description of Hera's beauty. Her actual name, Keftiu, is what we think the Egyptians called the Minoans.<br /> <br /> I've put entirely too much thought into this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T12:49:19-07:00","id":981627,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/968396-the-furry-thread#post968396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does anyone else here have experiences with the whole furry phenomenon, or have any characters they'd like to share? I'd obviously prefer this not become a gigantic dump of porn, bad art, and fetish sex stories, but things will probably take a mature turn. I'm curious to see where this winds up!</div> </div> </div> </div>A lot of my really good friends are furries.<br /> <br /> I think they get a massively bad rap, and people reduce them to the most extreme examples. Like, my boyfriend and I like attractive art of anthropomorphized animals and roleplaying - technically, that makes us low-grade furries.<br /> <br /> Even with the more extreme ones - for instance, people who claim to have &quot;the soul&quot; of an animal. If they're speaking literally, well, I'm a strict materialist, so I treat any spiritual claims as essentially meaningless, but I don't hold it against them. For the people who dress up in fur suits - I wouldn't do it, it looks a bit odd, but how is that my problem? If you enjoy it, more power to you.<br /> <br /> I've certainly never met one who thinks bestiality (defined as sex with a non-sapient, and therefore non-consenting by default, animal) is acceptable. I'm sure they exist, and <i>that's</i> a problem for animal abuse, but they aren't common, and that isn't a furry phenomenon.<br /> <br /> So really, all in all, what problem can a reasonable person possibly have with furries as a whole?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>We don't allow mages to cast spells, since this is the most unbalancing rule of all.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5226-jachra","name":"Jachra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T15:41:53-07:00","id":981741,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jachra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/968396-the-furry-thread?p=981627#post981627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Even with the more extreme ones - for instance, people who claim to have &amp;quot;the soul&amp;quot; of an animal. If they're speaking literally, well, I'm a strict materialist, so I treat any spiritual claims as essentially meaningless, but I don't hold it against them. </div> </div> </div> </div>It's worth pointing out that these otherkin/furries are pretty profoundly their own thing, and while some people are both or use furry as an outlet for these beliefs (I just recently made the acquaintance of one) to express something closer to what they feel their true self is. They're easy to judge (and I still raise an eyebrow at those who claim to be dragons or specific characters from media) but it becomes more palatable if you just view it as a niche spiritual belief.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T22:36:04-07:00","id":987625,"title":"","content":"Minor bump on the thread, but I got some <a href=\"http://imgur.com/a/jDQqt\" target=\"_blank\">new art</a> and I wanted to share it! (It's sfw, no worries!) <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T23:56:28-07:00","id":987651,"title":"","content":"Aww.... but I'm not at work!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T04:07:34-07:00","id":987701,"title":"","content":"I like those outfits, especially the goth one and the one that's kinda charleston with the feathers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T17:56:50-08:00","id":1002013,"title":"","content":"Distracting myself from both not being able to safely be out and from the general hell that is the world right now with a bunch of new artwork. Expect to see some of that soon.<br /> <br /> Also, I had a brief dream where I was my fursona, so that was more than a little weird.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T12:47:03-08:00","id":1006342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/968396-the-furry-thread?p=1002013#post1002013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Distracting myself from both not being able to safely be out and from the general hell that is the world right now with a bunch of new artwork. Expect to see some of that soon.<br /> <br /> Also, I had a brief dream where I was my fursona, so that was more than a little weird.</div> </div> </div> </div>And the first piece is done! I wanted something to articulate the pain of dysphoria and feeling wrong-bodied, and the result is pretty stunning. Minor nsfw warning for it <a href=\"http://atamajakki.tumblr.com/post/153463142539/so-i-got-a-really-lovely-piece-of-vent-art-from\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T13:01:25-08:00","id":1006349,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/968396-the-furry-thread?p=1006342#post1006342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And the first piece is done! I wanted something to articulate the pain of dysphoria and feeling wrong-bodied, and the result is pretty stunning. Minor nsfw warning for it <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;http://atamajakki.tumblr.com/post/153463142539/so-i-got-a-really-lovely-piece-of-vent-art-from&amp;quot;\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wow that came out great.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T21:10:53-08:00","id":1008404,"title":"","content":"Black Friday was hard, but I came home to this:<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/gWSpwpw.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":281,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","user":"atamajakki","date":". 11-26-2016, 12:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-26T06:00:47-08:00","id":1008505,"title":"","content":"Very cute! She seems so happy","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-10T11:28:22-07:00","id":1114219,"title":"","content":"I recently redesigned my fursona to look much like I do in reality and less idealized, and now one of my favorite artists has come out as a trans woman. This community is pretty horrible sometimes, but there's a lovely little space for queer representation amid the mess.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-10T13:20:07-07:00","id":1114254,"title":"","content":"Well,that seems like quite the step. Good for you!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T10:11:46-07:00","id":1115132,"title":"","content":"I tried to get into the furry fandom a while ago, but after some contemplation, I've decided it's really not for me. I've got nothing against the fandom and there's some genuinely good people in the fandom I know IRL, but I think any interest I may have had in the fandom was a passing interest at best.<br /> <br /> But others like it and that's okay. To each their own.<br /> <br /> That being said, I did have some ideas for a World War I RPG involving anthropomorphic animal characters. Sort of like &quot;The Wind In The Willows&quot; but with machine guns and mustard gas. Don't know if that counts as furry or not, but I thought it'd be worth mentioning that I still want to design that game one day.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1579,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","user":"Camilla","date":". 07-12-2017, 01:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T10:36:58-07:00","id":1115133,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Camilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/968396-the-furry-thread?p=1115132#post1115132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I tried to get into the furry fandom a while ago, but after some contemplation, I've decided it's really not for me. I've got nothing against the fandom and there's some genuinely good people in the fandom I know IRL, but I think any interest I may have had in the fandom was a passing interest at best.<br /> <br /> But others like it and that's okay. To each their own.<br /> <br /> That being said, I did have some ideas for a World War I RPG involving anthropomorphic animal characters. Sort of like &amp;quot;The Wind In The Willows&amp;quot; but with machine guns and mustard gas. Don't know if that counts as furry or not, but I thought it'd be worth mentioning that I still want to design that game one day.</div> </div> </div> </div>While not necessarily what I would consider furry, The Warren is an excellent PbtA game about talking rabbits and one of the settings is set on a WW1 battlefield. There's also Urban Jungle (I think?), the noir game by the Ironclaw folks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T10:49:17-07:00","id":1115137,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/968396-the-furry-thread?p=1115133#post1115133\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> While not necessarily what I would consider furry, The Warren is an excellent PbtA game about talking rabbits and one of the settings is set on a WW1 battlefield. There's also Urban Jungle (I think?), the noir game by the Ironclaw folks.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'll check those out, thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-12T21:24:03-08:00","id":1175682,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AzraelFirestorm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/968396-the-furry-thread?p=980009#post980009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Correct me if I'm way off base (and many apologies if I offend), but is there some psychological or thematic overlap with the Otherkin community and the Fur community? I'm thinking of a few things that seem like personal gray areas on this subject, when analyzing myself under a furred lens.<br /> <br /> Many thanks for any response!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> To put it in the most simplest of terms for newcomers, a Furry is merely somebody who enjoys the idea of anthropomorphic animals and there are a number of ways in which to explore / express that interest. The most common way is through writing and artwork which, contrary to what you may have been lead to believe, is not always porn related. In fact, I'm given to understand the pornographic side of the furry community is limited to a minority, as opposed to being part of the majority.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Otherkin</b>, however, are people who self-identify as a completely different species. They don't think of themselves as human, which has resulted in the <i>&quot;I identify as an Apache helicopter&quot;</i> meme that was made to mock and humiliate them. The furry community may indeed house a number of Otherkin who find it an easy way to express themselves in public, but they are not inherently the same thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-12T22:17:30-08:00","id":1175692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/968396-the-furry-thread?p=1175682#post1175682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> To put it in the most simplest of terms for newcomers, a Furry is merely somebody who enjoys the idea of anthropomorphic animals and there are a number of ways in which to explore / express that interest. The most common way is through writing and artwork which, contrary to what you may have been lead to believe, is not always porn related. In fact, I'm given to understand the pornographic side of the furry community is limited to a minority, as opposed to being part of the majority.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Otherkin</b>, however, are people who self-identify as a completely different species. They don't think of themselves as human, which has resulted in the <i>&amp;quot;I identify as an Apache helicopter&amp;quot;</i> meme that was made to mock and humiliate them. The furry community may indeed house a number of Otherkin who find it an easy way to express themselves in public, but they are not inherently the same thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>The attack helicopter meme has been appropriated by transphobic asshats. Also, I know some lovely otherkin; just think of it as a new age religion and it makes a lot more sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-12T22:51:27-08:00","id":1175698,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/968396-the-furry-thread?p=1175692#post1175692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The attack helicopter meme has been appropriated by transphobic asshats. Also, I know some lovely otherkin; just think of it as a new age religion and it makes a lot more sense.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Ehhh, calling it a religion might be bit of a stretch (<i>Ironic, seeing as I tried to start up a full blown cult in highschool</i>). But I can see it having elements of spiritualism to it. Still, I think a large part of the hate directed towards Otherkin stems from people seeing it as taking the fantasy a little bit too far. It's one thing to draw comics or write stories about you being turned into an anthropomorphic squirrel. It's something else completely to go around insisting that you are a squirrel in a man's body!<br /> <br /> <br /> This point of view isn't limited to just the Otherkin, though. Fur suiting is very popular in the furry community, and yet there are still those who consider the hobby to be a little bit on the creepy side. When you realize that most fur suiters design their own costumes and often spend thousands of dollars in order to do so, you can see why some people might have mixed feelings about it.<br /> <br /> <br /> Personally, I don't have a problem with either one of them. Given my current view of humanity in general, I'm not completely sure if I might be Otherkin or not. But whatever the situation, as long as the person in question isn't being obnoxious about it, I say just let them be who they want.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=z2_8cfVpXbo\" data-code=\"z2_8cfVpXbo\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/z2_8cfVpXbo/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 01-13-2018, 09:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-13T12:00:29-08:00","id":1175816,"title":"","content":"My new forum avatar is basically my male side's fursona. The only idealized part is me being able to afford a current console.<br /> <br /> here is a close up <img src=\"https://i.imgur.com/oTwNcjDm.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <br /> I have a whole bunch of other art from the same artist<br /> <br /> Like this Neanderthal cave werewolf (I like to think of him as my male fursona's prehistoric ancestor)<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://i.imgur.com/oQVW3qOm.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> My female side's fursona is here as a 50s housewife (which I have love for the aesthetics of when in female mode)<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://i.imgur.com/psWPoJem.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <br /> My latest drawing I got from him is this 80s corporate jerk werewolf<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://i.imgur.com/lB2vA9ym.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":3932,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","user":"The young man in the cafe","date":". 01-13-2018, 03:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-13T15:37:37-08:00","id":1175852,"title":"","content":"I don't think that deer is going to fit.<br /> <br /> Better get the bone saw!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-14T08:07:42-08:00","id":1175973,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/968396-the-furry-thread?p=1175852#post1175852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think that deer is going to fit.<br /> <br /> Better get the bone saw!</div> </div> </div> </div>Every werewolf needs to have one of those in the kitchen.<br /> <br /> And here is a drawing of a werewolf barista dealing with idiot customers at Snarlbucks drawn by the same artist as the others (Snarlbucks being the idea of a different artist named Teknicolor tiger)<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://i.imgur.com/VVtmRXEm.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-14T08:24:26-08:00","id":1175976,"title":"","content":"Oh by the way, if you guys haven't read the Subject 9 webcomic, I highly recommend checking it out.<br /> <br /> I don't know who the artist is (even though the artwork looks very familiar), but it was uploaded to youtube as a motion animated comic.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=tv4UPkM7ti4&amp;list=PLKnfGQdtTikopRY5IF_MJQEbUkJYRFVDg\" target=\"_blank\">This link</a> contains all 31 episodes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-24T19:27:55-08:00","id":1179058,"title":"","content":"This thread requires more love!<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://pre00.deviantart.net/5741/th/pre/i/2015/288/1/7/furry_road_by_kenket-d9d79ar.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-06T21:47:47-08:00","id":1183162,"title":"","content":"I've mainly been on the fringe of furrydom: for me, its not so much about having a \u201cfursona\u201d or dressing up in fur-suits or in any other way personally identifying with a kind of animal as it is about sapient animals in entertainment: the Wind in the Willows; Watership Down; Disney's Robin Hood, Talespin, Rescuers Down Under, Lady and the Tramp, Lion King, and others; Thundercats; My Little Pony; Palladium Books' Teenage Mutant Ninja Turtles and After the Bomb RPGs; Onyx Path's Pugmire and Monarchies of Mew; Big Ears Small Mouse; and so on. <br /> <br /> I would love to write and publish an RPG featuring a world of anthropomorphic animals, with no humans to be found even in legend, with character types spanning the full range of possibilities from elephants to mice and from sloths to cheetahs, and featuring both magic and superscience. Something like a cross between Zootopia and Thundercats. Thus far, only Palladium Books' furry-based games come anywhere close to what I'm looking for; and the game system is simply atrocious.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-07T06:40:03-08:00","id":1183241,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/968396-the-furry-thread?p=1183162#post1183162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've mainly been on the fringe of furrydom: for me, its not so much about having a \u201cfursona\u201d or dressing up in fur-suits or in any other way personally identifying with a kind of animal as it is about sapient animals in entertainment: the Wind in the Willows; Watership Down; Disney's Robin Hood, Talespin, Rescuers Down Under, Lady and the Tramp, Lion King, and others; Thundercats; My Little Pony; Palladium Books' Teenage Mutant Ninja Turtles and After the Bomb RPGs; Onyx Path's Pugmire and Monarchies of Mew; Big Ears Small Mouse; and so on.<br /> <br /> I would love to write and publish an RPG featuring a world of anthropomorphic animals, with no humans to be found even in legend, with character types spanning the full range of possibilities from elephants to mice and from sloths to cheetahs, and featuring both magic and superscience. Something like a cross between Zootopia and Thundercats. Thus far, only Palladium Books' furry-based games come anywhere close to what I'm looking for; and the game system is simply atrocious.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Well, I don't know about super science, but have you considered <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/145738/Furry-Pirates\" target=\"_blank\">Furry Pirates?</a><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=v4FigcghFy0\" data-code=\"v4FigcghFy0\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/v4FigcghFy0/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> I've also tried my hand at creating a number of free form style furry role playing games, but they always fizzled out. Often with players losing interest almost immediately after submitting their character sheets. Which simultaneously confused and infuriated me when I waited for them to hop into a game and they never showed back up again. There's only so many times you can dedicate weeks of passionate world building and lore write ups (only for nobody to care about it) before you lose the motivation to try again. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-20T05:52:49-08:00","id":1187815,"title":"","content":"More art from the artist I patreon<br /> <br /> Meet my 50s housewife fursona's greaser son and his girlfriend<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://i.imgur.com/hQov04Om.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-21T14:52:07-08:00","id":1188308,"title":"","content":"Would an RPG be considered &quot;furry&quot; just because it has anthropomorphic animals or is there more to it than that? I'm getting conflicting opinions on it from both sides, and I'm curious because I'm revisiting an idea of mine for a role-playing game involving anthropomorphic animal characters.<br /> <br /> The idea was called &quot;Trench Critters&quot; and based in World War I, originally envisioned as being like &quot;<i>The Wind In The Willows</i> but with machine guns and mustard gas&quot;, and I was initially worried about it being labeled as furry but that no longer bothers me. While I myself am not a furry in the traditional sense, I am comfortable with most furries and if people were to label my project as &quot;furry&quot;, that honestly would be okay with me so long as they like the game itself for what it is as a game system.<br /> <br /> I want to revisit the idea, but I am unsure if I should continue the World War I theme or do a different period of history. I've considered ideas for Ancient Rome, Dark Ages Europe and Medieval Fantasy (I suppose it'd be similar to Ironclaw), as well as the American Civil War and more recent conflicts like the Korean War and other Cold War events. I've got so many ideas I don't know what to do with them.<br /> <br /> Hell, you could even do a &quot;Furry Cyberpunk&quot; game and that could be good.<br /> <br /> While I don't have a fursona per se, I do have an interesting idea for a Trench Critters character that I have grown fond of. His name is Henry Anderson, and he is a young British infantry soldier in the trenches of the Western Front. His species is Ring-Necked Pheasant.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-21T16:18:57-08:00","id":1188327,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Camilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/968396-the-furry-thread?p=1188308#post1188308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would an RPG be considered &quot;furry&quot; just because it has anthropomorphic animals or is there more to it than that? I'm getting conflicting opinions on it from both sides, and I'm curious because I'm revisiting an idea of mine for a role-playing game involving anthropomorphic animal characters.<br /> <br /> The idea was called &quot;Trench Critters&quot; and based in World War I, originally envisioned as being like &quot;<i>The Wind In The Willows</i> but with machine guns and mustard gas&quot;, and I was initially worried about it being labeled as furry but that no longer bothers me. While I myself am not a furry in the traditional sense, I am comfortable with most furries and if people were to label my project as &quot;furry&quot;, that honestly would be okay with me so long as they like the game itself for what it is as a game system.<br /> <br /> I want to revisit the idea, but I am unsure if I should continue the World War I theme or do a different period of history. I've considered ideas for Ancient Rome, Dark Ages Europe and Medieval Fantasy (I suppose it'd be similar to Ironclaw), as well as the American Civil War and more recent conflicts like the Korean War and other Cold War events. I've got so many ideas I don't know what to do with them.<br /> <br /> Hell, you could even do a &quot;Furry Cyberpunk&quot; game and that could be good.<br /> <br /> While I don't have a fursona per se, I do have an interesting idea for a Trench Critters character that I have grown fond of. His name is Henry Anderson, and he is a young British infantry soldier in the trenches of the Western Front. His species is Ring-Necked Pheasant.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> Whether or not the game could be construed as 'furry' would come down to the individual players themselves, rather than some broad interpretation.<br /> <br /> As I previously explained, a furry is somebody who takes an interest in using anthropomorphic animals as a means of expressing themselves; hopefully in a good way, but every culture has its share of weirdos.<br /> <br /> <br /> If you're worried about the game being labeled as furry, I might suggest adding some additional sentient races, provided you have not already done so. If anthros are the only civilization walking around, then that could push the players to interpreting the game as being a furry universe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-21T19:50:07-08:00","id":1188381,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Camilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/968396-the-furry-thread?p=1188308#post1188308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would an RPG be considered &amp;quot;furry&amp;quot; just because it has anthropomorphic animals or is there more to it than that? I'm getting conflicting opinions on it from both sides, and I'm curious because I'm revisiting an idea of mine for a role-playing game involving anthropomorphic animal characters.<br /> <br /> The idea was called &amp;quot;Trench Critters&amp;quot; and based in World War I, originally envisioned as being like &amp;quot;<i>The Wind In The Willows</i> but with machine guns and mustard gas&amp;quot;, and I was initially worried about it being labeled as furry but that no longer bothers me. While I myself am not a furry in the traditional sense, I am comfortable with most furries and if people were to label my project as &amp;quot;furry&amp;quot;, that honestly would be okay with me so long as they like the game itself for what it is as a game system.<br /> <br /> I want to revisit the idea, but I am unsure if I should continue the World War I theme or do a different period of history. I've considered ideas for Ancient Rome, Dark Ages Europe and Medieval Fantasy (I suppose it'd be similar to Ironclaw), as well as the American Civil War and more recent conflicts like the Korean War and other Cold War events. I've got so many ideas I don't know what to do with them.<br /> <br /> Hell, you could even do a &amp;quot;Furry Cyberpunk&amp;quot; game and that could be good.<br /> <br /> While I don't have a fursona per se, I do have an interesting idea for a Trench Critters character that I have grown fond of. His name is Henry Anderson, and he is a young British infantry soldier in the trenches of the Western Front. His species is Ring-Necked Pheasant.</div> </div> </div> </div>Furry cyberpunk is super underrated, especially as transhumanist themes and ideas of body modification and queer identity expression expand further (fur-ther, haha!) into the genre. I know myself and no few number of my friends would look at least somewhat furry given the chance to. The intresting thing with that is not having an exclusively furry cyberpunk world, but rather having that be one of many axes of expression as freedom to truly liberate your body opens up; while a decent share of the world would be content looking like pretty humans (and we pity them for being so married to that tragic baseline), others would be furries, or chrome goddesses, or incomprehensible walking performance art - or a meld of all. That\u2019s the richest material in the modern cyberpunk genre to me, the questions of body and expression and identity and how technology influence that and open that up and tamp it down.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-21T19:58:20-08:00","id":1188384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/968396-the-furry-thread?p=1188381#post1188381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Furry cyberpunk is super underrated, especially as transhumanist themes and ideas of body modification and queer identity expression expand further (fur-ther, haha!) into the genre. I know myself and no few number of my friends would look at least somewhat furry given the chance to. The intresting thing with that is not having an exclusively furry cyberpunk world, but rather having that be one of many axes of expression as freedom to truly liberate your body opens up; while a decent share of the world would be content looking like pretty humans (and we pity them for being so married to that tragic baseline), others would be furries, or chrome goddesses, or incomprehensible walking performance art - or a meld of all. That\u2019s the richest material in the modern cyberpunk genre to me, the questions of body and expression and identity and how technology influence that and open that up and tamp it down.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://img00.deviantart.net/78c6/i/2014/115/c/2/meta_dragonart_the_cyberpunk_weasel_by_metadragonart-d7fxku4.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://pre00.deviantart.net/c8a2/th/pre/f/2016/095/1/d/you_just_keep_walking__buddy_by_metadragonart-d9xujhg.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-27T16:15:46-08:00","id":1190047,"title":"","content":"I got another drawing (more a sketch this time) of my male side's fursona, the chubby gamer werewolf. this time with a burger clutched in his paw/hand<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://i.imgur.com/xNDQfWYm.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signat