el=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, then I don't need to feel so bad about mine being too much of a special snowflake after all.</div> </div> </div> </div>I recommend you don't worry about that at all and just do what you want to do. Part of the point of it, right? ^.^","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-27T18:26:45-07:00","id":1230709,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/968396-the-furry-thread?p=1229946#post1229946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Soo I recently just discovered my inner furry and now want to have a fursona too, is it normal to have multiple fursona, or them not being animal (i.e alien, demon, fantasy creatures,..etc)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Of course! Some furries even have a tendency to change their fursona over the years once they get bored, or feel they identify more strongly with a new one.<br /> <br /> Take Immelmann, for example. They've been a rabbit, a wolf-rabbit, a horse, a pangolin, a velociraptor and even a martian!<br /> <br /> Not necessarily in that order, though.","signature":"","edited":{"u