der=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Feathery</b><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"https://images-wixmp-ed30a86b8c4ca887773594c2.wixmp.com/f/7c522d7f-36bd-42af-abd2-31071214de9d/d4q6v2y-d5c2c15f-c45c-4431-a783-3fe44f916a9c.jpg/v1/fill/w_900,h_1238,q_75,strp/harpy_by_carolina_eade_d4q6v2y-fullview.jpg?token=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9..3e5WQClDV03rlYDBYLOJOCDv8Qbck6GGkW9ryGWd5z0\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-25T11:59:42-07:00","id":1314332,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Camilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/968396-the-furry-thread?p=969824#post969824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I never really got into furry, though several of my close friends in real life are furries, so I don't have anything against furries. While it's not my cup of tea, I still don't understand the intense levels of vitriolic hatred the fandom gets online.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Yup, plus some forums and such on the internet that i will not name have discriminated against me for being a furry and have kicked me out and such.<br /> <br /> I wish the prejudice would stop against furries.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25351-axelthefox","name":"Axelthefox","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-01T12:50:23-08:00","id":1526208,"title":"","content":"Apologies for the thread necromancy, but I wanted to see if we had a furry thread before I decided to make one myself.<br /> <br /> I'm very delighted to see that we do.<br /> <br /> Yup, I am a fan of furry artwork, though I'm not that heavily involved in the fandom.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-04T21:58:48-07:00","id":1539826,"title":"","content":"It is actually kind of surreal to see some of the earlier posts given the situation with furries nowadays. Even back in 2016, furries were a known factor on the internet, but now it seems like they have reached the point of normalization where they are unremarkable. I think that that more than anything marks a huge psychological shift for how people in general see them. Granted, I think that that normalization effect applies mainly to people who regularly use the internet, but it is still significant to note. Back in the 2000s, furries were still seen as novel and strange. Regardless of how a person feels about them, they probably are just not surprised by them anymore. It has been fascinating to see this in action. It seems like a fair bit of knowledge regarding furry culture also gradually leaks out into other subcultures. I think that you especially see a lot of bleed in the role-playing game community, fantasy fandom, and sf fandom.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28352-verlan","name":"Verlan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"118"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-12T11:48:44-07:00","id":1540214,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verlan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/968396-the-furry-thread?p=1539826#post1539826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It seems like a fair bit of knowledge regarding furry culture also gradually leaks out into other subcultures. I think that you especially see a lot of bleed in the role-playing game community, fantasy fandom, and sf fandom.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hell, it's become mainstream enough that Last Week Tonight with John Oliver has made a recurring thing of alluding to the idea that John (or at least the persona he inhabits while presenting the show) is a furry, where the joke isn't really at the expense of that so much as the humour of the way he'd talk about implied interests.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-12T20:42:24-07:00","id":1540259,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/968396-the-furry-thread?p=1540214#post1540214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hell, it's become mainstream enough that Last Week Tonight with John Oliver has made a recurring thing of alluding to the idea that John (or at least the persona he inhabits while presenting the show) is a furry, where the joke isn't really at the expense of that so much as the humour of the way he'd talk about implied interests.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is actually surreal to hear. It always seemed like the way mainstream media outlets covered furries has not changed for a good two decades. The fact that a joke like that can be tossed around without immediately explaining what furries are says a lot about the context the audience is already expected to know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28352-verlan","name":"Verlan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"118"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-19T11:54:40-08:00","id":1558384,"title":"","content":"Now is not the time for sadness.<br /> <br /> Now is the time for Yinglets.<br /> <br /> Artist is MentalCrash<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTag